  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "An open box is constructed by starting with a rectangular sheet of metal \\(10\\) in. by \\(14\\) in. and cutting a square of side \\(x\\) inches from each corner. The resulting projections are folded up and the seams welded. The volume of the resulting box is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(140x-48x^2+4x^3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(140x+48x^2+4x^3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(140x+24x^2+x^3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(140x-24x^2+x^3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "none of these"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1957-p6.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The box has height \\(x\\) and base dimensions \\(10-2x\\) and \\(14-2x.\\) Hence \\[ \\begin{aligned} V&=x(10-2x)(14-2x)\\\\ &=140x-48x^2+4x^3. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "After folding, the height is \\(x\\) and each base dimension loses \\(2x\\)",
        "Write the volume as \\(x(10-2x)(14-2x)\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
